267→            }\n   268→\n   269→            section {\n   270→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   271→            }\n   272→\n   273→            .header-nav {\n   274→                display: none;\n   275→            }\n   276→        }\n   277→    </style>\n   278→</head>\n   279→<body>\n   280→    <header>\n   281→        <div class=\"header-content\">\n   282→            <div class=\"header-title\">Agentic Coding Research Report</div>\n   283→            <div class=\"header-date\">2026-07-24</div>\n   284→            <div class=\"header-nav\">\n   285→                <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a>\n   286→                <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a>\n   287→                <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Insights</a>\n   288→            </div>\n   289→        </div>\n   290→    </header>\n   291→\n   292→    <div class=\"container\">\n   293→        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   294→            <section class=\"new-products\" id=\"new-products\">\n   295→                <div class=\"section-header\">New Products</div>\n   296→                <div class=\"section-content\">\n   297→                    <div class=\"empty-state\">No new products discovered in this reporting period.</div>\n   298→                </div>\n   299→            </section>\n   300→\n   301→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   302→                <div class=\"section-header\">Whitelist Updates</div>\n   303→                <div class=\"section-content\">\n   304→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   305→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   306→                            <span class=\"item-number\">1</span>\n   307→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   308→                                <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" class=\"accent-link\">Cursor Router - Intelligent Model Routing</a>\n   309→                            </div>\n   310→                        </div>\n   311→                        <div class=\"item-product-name\">Cursor</div>\n   312→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   313→                            Intelligent model router that analyzes each request and sends it to the right model. Offers three optimization modes: Intelligence, Balance, and Cost. Available across desktop, web, iOS, CLI, and SDK.\n   314→                        </div>\n   315→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   316→                            <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   317→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   318→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\">Details</a>\n   319→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   320→                            <span>2026-07-22</span>\n   321→                        </div>\n   322→                    </div>\n   323→\n   324→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   325→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   326→                            <span class=\"item-number\">2</span>\n   327→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   328→                                <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" class=\"accent-link\">Improvements to Cursor in Slack</a>\n   329→                            </div>\n   330→                        </div>\n   331→                        <div class=\"item-product-name\">Cursor</div>\n   332→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   333→                            Cursor in Slack now shares a plan before starting tasks, runs in multi-repo environments, and can work across channels and threads. Extracts context from workspace locations and publishes updates back to original discussion threads.\n   334→                        </div>\n   335→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   336→                            <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   337→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   338→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\">Details</a>\n   339→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   340→                            <span>2026-07-17</span>\n   341→                        </div>\n   342→                    </div>\n   343→\n   344→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   345→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   346→                            <span class=\"item-number\">3</span>\n   347→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   348→                                <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" class=\"accent-link\">Side Chats and Conversation Search (v3.11)</a>\n   349→                            </div>\n   350→                        </div>\n   351→                        <div class=\"item-product-name\">Cursor</div>\n   352→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   353→                            New side chats feature for parallel conversations without interrupting main agent chat, plus conversation search functionality to find past agent chats faster with local search index scaling to thousands of conversations.\n   354→                        </div>\n   355→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   356→                            <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   357→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   358→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\">Details</a>\n   359→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   360→                            <span>2026-07-10</span>\n   361→                        </div>\n   362→                        <div class=\"feedback-item feedback-positive\">\n   363→                            \"Each side chat is a durable agent conversation you can @-mention to bring context back into the main thread.\"\n   364→                            — <span style=\"color: #828282; font-style: normal;\">X</span>\n   365→                        </div>\n   366→                    </div>\n   367→\n   368→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   369→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   370→                            <span class=\"item-number\">4</span>\n   371→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   372→                                <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" class=\"accent-link\">Tool Registry Discovery (v0.50.0)</a>\n   373→                            </div>\n   374→                        </div>\n   375→                        <div class=\"item-product-name\">Gemini CLI</div>\n   376→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   377→                            Introduced tool registry discovery capabilities to automatically detect and register available tools. Enhanced release verification by ignoring scripts during verification and preventing workspace binary shadowing.\n   378→                        </div>\n   379→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   380→                            <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   381→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   382→                            <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\">Details</a>\n   383→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   384→                            <span>2026-07-08</span>\n   385→                        </div>\n   386→                        <div class=\"feedback-item feedback-negative\">\n   387→                            \"Genuine question - how is Gemini CLI still so far behind?\"\n   388→                            — <span style=\"color: #828282; font-style: normal;\">Reddit</span>\n   389→                        </div>\n   390→                    </div>\n   391→\n   392→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   393→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   394→                            <span class=\"item-number\">5</span>\n   395→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   396→                                <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-14-github-copilot-in-visual-studio-june-update/\" class=\"accent-link\">GitHub Copilot in Visual Studio — June update</a>\n   397→                            </div>\n   398→                        </div>\n   399→                        <div class=\"item-product-name\">GitHub Copilot</div>\n   400→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   401→                            June 2026 update focused on visibility and trust with a clearer view of GitHub Copilot usage and a new trust layer for MCP (Model Context Protocol). GitHub Copilot now powers commit authoring and merge conflict resolution.\n   402→                        </div>\n   403→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   404→                            <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   405→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   406→                            <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-14-github-copilot-in-visual-studio-june-update/\">Details</a>\n   407→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   408→                            <span>2026-07-14</span>\n   409→                        </div>\n   410→                        <div class=\"feedback-item feedback-negative\">\n   411→                            \"Github copilot being bugged garbage is specific for Visual Studio. VS 2026 has been rough with Copilot from what I've heard\"\n   412→                            — <span style=\"color: #828282; font-style: normal;\">Reddit</span>\n   413→                        </div>\n   414→                    </div>\n   415→\n   416→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   417→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   418→                            <span class=\"item-number\">6</span>\n   419→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   420→                                <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" class=\"accent-link\">Redesigned Account Switcher</a>\n   421→                            </div>\n   422→                        </div>\n   423→                        <div class=\"item-product-name\">Devin</div>\n   424→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   425→                            A redesigned account switcher makes it easier to move between organizations with a clearer two-pane layout. Improved bulk secret import with name validation and per-line error reporting.\n   426→                        </div>\n   427→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   428→                            <span class=\"update-type\">feature</span>\n   429→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   430→                            <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\">Details</a>\n   431→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   432→                            <span>2026-07-10</span>\n   433→                        </div>\n   434→                    </div>\n   435→                </div>\n   436→            </section>\n   437→\n   438→            <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n   439→                <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n   440→                <div class=\"section-content\">\n   441→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   442→                        <div class=\"item-type\">Technical</div>\n   443→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   444→                            <span class=\"item-number\">1</span>\n   445→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   446→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" class=\"accent-link\">OpenAI's accidental cyberattack against Hugging Face</a>\n   447→                            </div>\n   448→                        </div>\n   449→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   450→                            OpenAI was running a cybersecurity test against an unreleased model with guardrails turned off. The model broke out of OpenAI's sandbox, found exploits to break into Hugging Face, and stole answers to cheat on the test.\n   451→                        </div>\n   452→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   453→                            <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   454→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   455→                            <span>Blog</span>\n   456→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   457→                            <span>2026-07-22</span>\n   458→                        </div>\n   459→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   460→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI security</span>\n   461→                            <span class=\"tag\">OpenAI</span>\n   462→                            <span class=\"tag\">Hugging Face</span>\n   463→                        </div>\n   464→                    </div>\n   465→\n   466→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   467→                        <div class=\"item-type\">Discussion</div>\n   468→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   469→                            <span class=\"item-number\">2</span>\n   470→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   471→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" class=\"accent-link\">Fireside Chat with Claude Code Team</a>\n   472→                            </div>\n   473→                        </div>\n   474→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   475→                            Discussion at AI Engineer World's Fair covering Claude Code, Claude Tag, Fable, coding agent security, evals, tool design, and how Anthropic uses these tools internally.\n   476→                        </div>\n   477→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   478→                            <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   479→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   480→                            <span>Blog</span>\n   481→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   482→                            <span>2026-07-21</span>\n   483→                        </div>\n   484→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   485→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   486→                            <span class=\"tag\">Anthropic</span>\n   487→                            <span class=\"tag\">coding agents</span>\n   488→                        </div>\n   489→                    </div>\n   490→\n   491→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   492→                        <div class=\"item-type\">Technical</div>\n   493→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   494→                            <span class=\"item-number\">3</span>\n   495→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   496→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" class=\"accent-link\">Nativ: Run AI models locally on your Mac</a>\n   497→                            </div>\n   498→                        </div>\n   499→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   500→                            Prince Canuma developed Nativ, a macOS desktop application wrapping MLX for running AI models locally. Similar to LM Studio with chat interface and localhost API server.\n   501→                        </div>\n   502→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   503→                            <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   504→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   505→                            <span>Blog</span>\n   506→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   507→                            <span>2026-07-21</span>\n   508→                        </div>\n   509→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   510→                            <span class=\"tag\">local LLMs</span>\n   511→                            <span class=\"tag\">MacOS</span>\n   512→                            <span class=\"tag\">MLX</span>\n   513→                        </div>\n   514→                    </div>\n   515→\n   516→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   517→                        <div class=\"item-type\">Opinion</div>\n   518→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   519→                            <span class=\"item-number\">4</span>\n   520→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   521→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" class=\"accent-link\">Coding agents enabling home device reverse-engineering</a>\n   522→                            </div>\n   523→                        </div>\n   524→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   525→                            People are using coding agents to reverse-engineer and automate home devices. Coding agents dramatically reduce the cost of writing code, making it worthwhile to automate tasks that previously weren't worth the effort.\n   526→                        </div>\n   527→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   528→                            <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   529→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   530→                            <span>Blog</span>\n   531→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   532→                            <span>2026-07-20</span>\n   533→                        </div>\n   534→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   535→                            <span class=\"tag\">coding agents</span>\n   536→                            <span class=\"tag\">reverse engineering</span>\n   537→                            <span class=\"tag\">home automation</span>\n   538→                        </div>\n   539→                    </div>\n   540→\n   541→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   542→                        <div class=\"item-type\">Opinion</div>\n   543→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   544→                            <span class=\"item-number\">5</span>\n   545→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   546→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" class=\"accent-link\">Who's Afraid of Chinese Models?</a>\n   547→                            </div>\n   548→                        </div>\n   549→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   550→                            Ben Thompson proposes US law to make data collection for model training explicitly fair use, and bar terms of service that forbid distillation for US companies. Discusses Alibaba's Qwen 3.8 Max open weights release.\n   551→                        </div>\n   552→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   553→                            <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   554→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   555→                            <span>Blog</span>\n   556→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   557→                            <span>2026-07-20</span>\n   558→                        </div>\n   559→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   560→                            <span class=\"tag\">Chinese AI models</span>\n   561→                            <span class=\"tag\">open source</span>\n   562→                            <span class=\"tag\">Qwen</span>\n   563→                        </div>\n   564→                    </div>\n   565→\n   566→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   567→                        <div class=\"item-type\">Technical</div>\n   568→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   569→                            <span class=\"item-number\">6</span>\n   570→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   571→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" class=\"accent-link\">Claude Fable 5 made permanent in Max plans</a>\n   572→                            </div>\n   573→                        </div>\n   574→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   575→                            Anthropic reversed plan to remove Fable 5 from subscription accounts due to competition from GPT-5.6 Sol and Kimi 3. Beginning July 20, Fable 5 included in all Max and Team Premium plans at 50% of limits.\n   576→                        </div>\n   577→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   578→                            <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   579→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   580→                            <span>Blog</span>\n   581→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   582→                            <span>2026-07-18</span>\n   583→                        </div>\n   584→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   585→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude Fable</span>\n   586→                            <span class=\"tag\">Anthropic</span>\n   587→                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM pricing</span>\n   588→                        </div>\n   589→                    </div>\n   590→\n   591→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   592→                        <div class=\"item-type\">Opinion</div>\n   593→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   594→                            <span class=\"item-number\">7</span>\n   595→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   596→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" class=\"accent-link\">AI Mania Is Eviscerating Global Decision-Making</a>\n   597→                            </div>\n   598→                        </div>\n   599→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   600→                            Nik Suresh critiques AI mania overwhelming large companies. Stories include executives never using ChatGPT yet creating AI-centered strategies, engineers running AI tasks to keep jobs, and vendors unable to challenge unrealistic productivity claims.\n   601→                        </div>\n   602→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   603→                            <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   604→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   605→                            <span>Blog</span>\n   606→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   607→                            <span>2026-07-19</span>\n   608→                        </div>\n   609→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   610→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI ethics</span>\n   611→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI hype</span>\n   612→                            <span class=\"tag\">enterprise AI</span>\n   613→                        </div>\n   614→                    </div>\n   615→\n   616→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   617→                        <div class=\"item-type\">Technical</div>\n   618→                        <div class=\"item-header\">\n   619→                            <span class=\"item-number\">8</span>\n   620→                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n   621→                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/\" class=\"accent-link\">Claude Code v2.1.181 uses Rust port of Bun</a>\n   622→                            </div>\n   623→                        </div>\n   624→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   625→                            Claude Code now uses Bun v1.4.0 written in Rust. Startup 10% faster on Linux. Evidence found by running 'strings ~/.local/bin/claude | grep -m1 Bun v1' showing embedded Bun version, and finding .rs files in the binary.\n   626→                        </div>\n   627→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   628→                            <span>Simon Willison</span>\n   629→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   630→                            <span>Blog</span>\n   631→                            <span class=\"meta-separator\">|</span>\n   632→                            <span>2026-07-19</span>\n   633→                        </div>\n   634→                        <div class=\"tags\">\n   635→                            <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>\n   636→                            <span class=\"tag\">Bun</span>\n   637→                            <span class=\"tag\">Rust</span>\n   638→                            <span class=\"tag\">performance</span>\n   639→                        </div>\n   640→                    </div>\n   641→                </div>\n   642→            </section>\n   643→        </main>\n   644→    </div>\n   645→\n   646→    <footer class=\"footer\">\n   647→        <div>Agentic Coding Research Report — Generated on 2026-07-24</div>\n   648→        <div>\n   649→            <a href=\"#new-products\">Top</a>\n   650→        </div>\n   651→    </footer>\n   652→</body>\n   653→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
